    \item [$\Leftarrow$:] we now show how to transform any {\clawpathdecomp} $D'$ of $G'$ into a decomposition of $(G, M)$. Again, the only parts of $D'$ that will need adapting are those connected to the co-fishes that we inserted when transforming $G$ into $G'$. 
